\title{hydrofabric: Build Hydrologic Modeling Fabrics from Reference Networks}
\description{
A general toolkit for building hydrologic modeling fabrics from a reference hydrographic network. Flowlines are split, collapsed, and reconciled against flow direction and flow accumulation rasters; catchment divides are partitioned to match; the network is aggregated to a distribution topology; and per-unit results are merged into global domains with globally unique identifiers. Outputs are checked against structural invariants and stamped with build provenance for reproducible reuse. The reference application is the NOAA Office of Water Prediction National Water Model (NWM) v4 for the NextGen Modeling System, developed with partial OWP funding.
